# Code Review Checklist

Before considering a task done, verify:

## Correctness
- [ ] Change works across difficulty levels 1–5 when game logic is touched
- [ ] Mobile (≤640px) and desktop layouts still behave correctly
- [ ] Login, game flow, leaderboard, and favorites paths are unaffected (or intentionally updated)

## Quality
- [ ] No quick fixes: root cause addressed, not symptoms patched
- [ ] No unrelated files or drive-by refactors
- [ ] Existing comments preserved
- [ ] New code follows BEM + `js-` hook separation
- [ ] French UI strings unchanged unless the task requires copy changes

## Safety
- [ ] localStorage read/write errors are handled, not ignored
- [ ] No secrets or credentials added to committed files
- [ ] No `!important` or inline-style workarounds without justification

## If Blocked

When a proper fix needs architectural change (e.g. splitting `script.js`, removing jQuery, env-based config), **stop and propose the plan to Pierre** rather than shipping a workaround.
